WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.280
- Our show wants to be a place

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.240
where we can come together and
build genuine relationships.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.660
Have real conversations
and lift one another up.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.670
So when I saw our next
guest creating an initiative

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.290
doing just that, I knew
we had to chat with her!

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.770
Take a look.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.680
- Hi, my name is Luuvie Ajayi Jones

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.350
and I am a writer, a
speaker, a podcast host

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.920
and I am also one of the four women

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.030
who've created the Share
The Mic Now campaign.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.393
Shout out to my fellow
creators and founders,

00:00:29.393 --> 00:00:33.090
Bozoma Saint John, Glennon
Doyle and Stacey Bendet.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.600
As we search to figure out
allies should look like,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.820
we decide to ask prominent white women

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.330
that we are in community with

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.010
to hand over their
Instagram accounts for a day

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.270
to black women who
typically might not have

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.670
that major platform.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.400
Because when the world listens to women,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.437
it listens to white women.

00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:51.060
And it is time for black women's
voices to be given space.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:51.980
Over the course of a week,

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.453
we had 50 black women agree
to take over the accounts

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:57.300
of 50 white women and tell their stories,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.890
amplify their voices,
talk about their lives

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.280
and their experiences,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.820
because we wanted to show
what community could look like

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.750
and sisterhood in action.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.137
Our hope with Share The Mic Now,

00:01:07.137 --> 00:01:09.370
was to catalyze a change that only happens

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.593
when we truly listen
to each other's voices.

00:01:14.215 --> 00:01:18.607
- And now ladies and gentlemen,
Luuvie Ajayi Jones, Luuvie!

00:01:20.043 --> 00:01:21.130
(audience applauding)
- Hi Drew!

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.350
- Now, can you share with me,

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.150
this was such an exciting question

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.510
for me to just get right in.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:29.700
How did you select the women you chose

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.733
to start this initiative with?

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.790
- Yeah, when we decide
to do Share The Mic Now,

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.990
we were like, we wanna pick women

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:39.960
who have already used
their voices in some way

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.430
to speak up about racial justice.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.180
You know, they're the
people who've already said

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.460
Black Lives Matter.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.960
So, me and Boz got with Glennon and said,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.110
let's do this in this big way.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.877
Glennon said, "Okay I'll be back.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.887
"I'll go talk to some
white women who I respect

00:01:52.887 --> 00:01:54.510
"and see if they'll say yes."

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.217
And Glennon went and said,

00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:58.187
"Hey, I just need you to hand
over your Instagram account

00:01:58.187 --> 00:02:02.360
"for a day to a black woman
who's amazing, are you down?"

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.070
And everyone said yes to that question.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.380
She would come back and be like,

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.000
Hillary Clinton just said yes,
Brene Brown just said yes,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.260
Jen Hatmaker just said yes.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.930
And for us, once we had the white women

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.838
who were prominent confirmed,
we went to black women

00:02:15.838 --> 00:02:19.860
who's voices we really loved
and who's voices needed

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.820
bigger platforms to be heard.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.450
- How did you pair the women?

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.330
'Cause I thought that process, to me,

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.190
was really interesting as well.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.790
- So we actually called up Zoom,

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.150
and had everyone join us.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.670
I'm thinking assistants
were going to join us,

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.370
but when I'm seeing Yaba Blay join,

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.960
when I'm seeing Tarana Burke,
and I'm seeing Ashley Judd,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.300
all without makeup at seven
o'clock in the morning,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.640
I'm like this is special.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.220
And we decided to pair people up

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.960
based on industry, who we
thought were easily matched

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.150
like Gwyneth Paltrow and Latham Thomas.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.660
Or chemistry, like Esther
Perel and Yvette Noel-Schure.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.344
So we created those pairs

00:02:52.344 --> 00:02:55.040
and just hoped the magic would happen

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.370
and magic did happen,
because some of these pairs

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.730
are now collaborators, like
they've worked together.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.090
They're continuing to talk,

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.960
they have actually built
friendship with each other.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.960
- And actually we're gonna
share the mic today together.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:12.420
Who are we collaborating
with today, Luuvie?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.070
- So I think someone
amazing is Rachel Rodgers.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.320
She is a mom of four, she is a wife,

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.790
she is just an overall dope woman.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.260
And her company, Hello 7
empowers entrepreneurial women

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.800
to become millionaires
without losing their sanity.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.190
And she's somebody who is worth
us sharing the mic now with.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:30.790
- Please welcome Rachel Rodgers!

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.848
(audience applauding)

00:03:34.848 --> 00:03:35.986
- [All] Oh!

00:03:35.986 --> 00:03:37.320
- Oh, hi Rachel!

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.700
Thank you so much for coming on the show!

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.280
- Thank you so much for having me.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.050
- Tell us about your
business, Hello 7, Rachel.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.584
- So, what I do is I work
with women entrepreneurs,

00:03:47.584 --> 00:03:50.660
and what I saw is so much conversation

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.230
in the women's entrepreneur market

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.900
about getting to six
figures, getting to 100K.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.280
And I'm like, I don't know
if y'all been at 100K,

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.320
but it's not enough money, you know?

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:02.700
I'm like, no, why are we
setting our goals so low?

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.000
Let's go for a million!

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.340
Let's build seven figure businesses.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.070
And so I just started talking about it

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.170
and I started teaching
it, because I really saw

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.990
that a lot of the training out there

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:14.350
just got you to six figures
but it didn't teach you

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.510
how to get to seven
figures and how to build

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:17.770
a million dollar business.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:19.350
There was like, no advanced training

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.200
that was focused on women.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.900
And so I decided to create that.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.460
So that's what we do at Hello
7, and it's a lot of fun.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.830
We really enjoy it.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.660
- We live in a society, that talks about

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.220
you can have it all, the
mantra out there, I think,

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.930
makes us feel like, it
is all on our shoulders.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.550
- Absolutely. Listen,
I make it very clear.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.290
I'm not trying to be all
things for my children,

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:46.670
for my husband, even for my business.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.120
It's crazy how, even bread-winning women,

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.210
are always the ones

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:52.990
doing the bulk of the domestic work.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.760
And so, for me I'm like listen,

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.540
I wanna be there to parent my children,

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.050
but I don't need to do their
laundry, and clean for them

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.530
and cook for them and
do everything for them.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.020
So, I make them part of the conversation

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:08.260
and I trust that they can
handle that and understand that.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:12.880
- I am so honored to share
the mic with you today Rachel.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.710
Luuvie, I would love to ask you,

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.710
can this be a place that
we can continue and foster

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.910
this incredible initiative
that you have launched

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.930
and been a game changer for?

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:25.860
- I would love that.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.310
I think your platform and who
you represent in this world

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:32.130
is significant and you've been
able to share the mic now,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.360
with women who typically
don't have this platform,

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.910
is part of the action that we can take

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:39.050
to change the world.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:42.350
- I am honored and humbled to do so,

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.833
and all I can say is, let's do this.

00:05:44.833 --> 00:05:47.416
(upbeat music)

